I focused first on the actual port‐mismatch in the wrapper instantiation (which is what Xcelium complained about), then on the two places that drive and declare the narrower PMP‐address bus (the CS‐register file and the RVFI package), and finally on the top‐level CV32E40S module where the RVFI bus is originally defined.

```
// 1) Fix the port connection/zero‐extension in the RTL wrapper
rtl/cv32e40s/bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv

// 2) (Optional) widen or parameterize the pmp_addr_rdata declaration
rtl/cv32e40s/rtl/cs_registers.sv

// 3) Align the RVFI pmpaddr signal width to match (or parameterize) PMP_ADDR_WIDTH
rtl/rvfi/rvfi_pkg.sv

// 4) Update the RVFI bus definition in the core itself if needed
rtl/cv32e40s/rtl/cv32e40s.sv
```
